{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/328329-fire-and-water-the-river-of-death-open-dev","id":328329,"title":"Fire and Water: The River of Death (Open Dev)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-02T09:56:22-08:00","id":328329,"title":"Fire and Water: The River of Death (Open Dev)","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-river-of-death-promethean-the-created/\" target=\"_blank\">New blog's up.</a><br /> <br /> In my characteristic fashion, a neat bit of maybe-salient reading:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Central Fire</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://web.eecs.utk.edu/~mclennan/BA/AGEDE/Fire.html#CF\" target=\"_blank\">Having considered Fire in the microcosm, we now turn to the macrocosm.</a> According to the Pythagoreans, the Enveloping Fire is balanced by a Central Fire. <b>Indeed, Empedocles says that many fires burn beneath the Earth, that the Solar Fire was born in the bowels of the Earth, and that Volcanic Fire shoots to the Heavens and licks the stars. Thus Fire is the highest and the lowest Element;</b> it is as though the Elemental Square has been unfolded into a line (<a href=\"https://web.eecs.utk.edu/~mclennan/BA/AGEDE/images/central-fire.gif\" target=\"_blank\">see figure</a>). This results in a series of cosmic spheres: Celestial Fire, Air, Water, Earth, and Central Fire; the Celestial Fire mirrors the Central Fire as though in a higher octave.<br /> <br /> One might suppose that the &quot;Fires of Hades&quot; is a Christian notion, but it actually has its roots in ancient Greek esoteric doctrine. As explained in the &quot;Introduction&quot; and in &quot;Earth,&quot; &quot;Water&quot; and &quot;Air,&quot; Empedocles' &quot;Enigma&quot; associates Earth with Hera, Water with Persephone, Air with Zeus, and Fire with Hades. <b>However, there are many additional signposts to the Central Fire, for Empedocles teaches that the ultimate source of all Fire is Hades, and that the Central Fire is the source of all life, creation and destruction (see &quot;Hephaistos and Alchemy,&quot; below).</b><br /> <br /> More precisely, the Central Fire is Tartaros, Zeus's Guard Tower (Zan\u00f2s P\u00fargos, Phulak\u00ea Di\u00f3s, etc.), which is below Hades. <b>According to myth, after the Sun sets, it shines in Tartaros. Therefore the Central Fire is known as the Dark Sun, the Black Sun, the Invisible Sun, the Subterranean Sun and the Volcanic Sun, and there is a paradoxical unity between the Sun and the Underworld.</b> This is why Parmenides was led by the Daughters of the Sun into the House of Night; it is also the path followed by the dead.<br /> <br /> <b>The astrological symbol for the Sun represents the Fire at the center; it was also an ancient alchemical symbol for Sulphur, the Fiery Principle (on which, see below).</b> The doctrine of the Central Fire is the original, mystical Heliocentric theory, which Copernicus borrowed, but has become debased into no more than astronomy. (Copernicus himself called it the &quot;Pythagorean Theory.&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T10:43:40-08:00","id":328406,"title":"","content":"I like the fact that all Prometheans have to die at least once, if not due to the problems along the Pilgrimage then at the very peak of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T11:39:01-08:00","id":328478,"title":"","content":"I always loved running the River of Death scenes in my games. Now it's a universal milestone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T19:05:49-08:00","id":328829,"title":"","content":"I like that all Prometheans must die to achieve the New Dawn as well. It's perfect, in a mystical way. The only way to gain true life is to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T19:10:55-08:00","id":328832,"title":"","content":"It feels so organic I wonder why no one did anything with it in the old version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T10:14:51-08:00","id":329330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/328329-fire-and-water-the-river-of-death-open-dev?p=328832#post328832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels so organic I wonder why no one did anything with it in the old version.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the Rivers of Death didn't really get quantified until Geist, so that's probably part of the reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T11:21:16-08:00","id":330357,"title":"","content":"Definitely going to use the opportunity for a Promethean to meet the ghosts of the humans whose bodies she's made out of!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T13:37:46-08:00","id":334512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/328329-fire-and-water-the-river-of-death-open-dev?p=329330#post329330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Rivers of Death didn't really get quantified until Geist, so that's probably part of the reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was specifically as a hope to bring more meat to my <b>Promethean</b> game that I looked at <i>World of Darkness: Book of the Dead</i> in the first place.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't know aught of what <b>Geist</b> is about other than some ghost-stuff is in there, but I AM a huge fan of the classic World of Darkness game <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b>. Yes, the entire milieu of the Underworld is different from the two worlds, but I'd felt that the lands of dead really received short shrift before <b>Geist</b> came along. Yeah, yeah, yeah, I know that the whole notion of the Tempest and Stygia and whatnot from <b>Wraith</b> are a hard fit with First Edition World of Darkness, but this post about River of Death experiences gives me some hope for the Underworld getting a little more overall attention in Second Edition!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}